  "overview": "Overview",
  "@overview": {},
  "preMonsoonOverviewText": "Nigeria's cashew belt faces its highest disease pressure of the year once the rains begin, typically in April. Anthracnose, Gumosis, and Red Rust all thrive in the warm, humid, wet conditions that follow and by the time symptoms are obvious, treatment is playing catch-up. This guide covers the preparation farmers should complete in March, before the rains start, so your trees enter the wet season with disease pressure already reduced.",
  "@preMonsoonOverviewText": {},
